JOIN THE BATTLE OF IDEAS
________________________
The Intercollegiate Studies Institute (ISI) has more than 40,000 student and 
faculty members who, in addition to other benefits, receive "CAMPUS" and "The 
Intercollegiate Review" at no charge. ISI is a non-profit educational 
organization that has been carrying out a very specific program since 1953.

ISI works closely with over 2,100 student Campus Representative and Faculty 
Associates, articulating the importance of a traditional liberal arts education
rooted in the Western heritage. ISI believes that if America is to prosper as a
free society, her young people must have a solid understanding and respect for 
the ideas and institutions that make America great.

These special ISI representatives introduce fellow students and faculty to ISI,
promote ISI publications and programs, and arrange ISI lectures on their 
campus.

ISI reaches more than 100,000 students at 1,000 colleges and universities 
through its publications and lecture programs. Through these programs, ISI is 
effecting reform in the academy.

ISI PROGRAMS

* ISI publishes "CAMPUS" and the "Intercollegiate Review", as well as "Modern 
Age" and "The Political Science Reviewer."

* A National lecture program that holds 250 lecture annually on college 
campuses.

* 20 educational conferences, seminars, and summer schools held around the 
country each year.

* $140,000 a year in fellowships to graduate students who intend to pursue 
