If it weren't for the demonstrated impotence of that particular policy
(and the fact that *all* such policies are subject to review in an
open meeting), I'd be more interested in continuing this discussion.

>It sounds like you have created a very efficient and useful system
>for the entire university community.

Um, not exactly.  We're not, and never have been, a system serving the
entire university community (with a few exceptions); the vast majority
of our resources are restricted to our users, who comprise the CIS
community.  The general university community is serviced by the Magnus
system run by Academic Computing Services (remember them?).

>A bitmap directory is a very very good idea from the point of view of
