I believe we are all fumbling in the dark. University administrators
often know little of computers. Faculty and student computer users
often know little of the sys admins' experience. Sys admin often know
little of academic and intellectual freedom. The only way to light the
darkness, to counter misconceptions, and to avoid bad policies is to
share, discuss, debate, and learn.

I'm enclosing pointers to several computer polices and policy
suggestions based in part on library principles. Your critique is
welcome.

- Carl

