WRONG!  It only applies to NSFNet sites.  It sure doesn't apply to my site,
I follow the DDN(Milnet) AUP.  It doesn't apply to PSINet or Alternet sites
or any of the other commerical service providers, they all have their own
AUPs.  Misc.forsale is a newsgroup.  Like other newsgroups it gets to sites
via a variety of methods including direct, private, dial-up links.  If it
does travel over NSFNet or any other network with an AUP that forbids that
type of article, then it is the injecting site's responsibility to filter
that article.  In practice this is rarely done since it is a virtual
impossibility.

Once again:  Usenet (the collection of sites that carry the various
newsgroups) != {NSFNet || Milnet || BARNet || Internet (sum total of all
interconnected IP networks)}.  It is a cooperative anarchy with a set of
guidelines adhered to by convention.  There is no governing body,
"enforcement" is by peer pressure.

Now, as to what is acceptable in the various misc.forsale groups:  whatever
the readership will permit.

