Not that I've heard of. In the U.S., the Supreme Court's public forum
doctrine allows restrictions on access to government-owned created
forums. For example, as a student at U. of Illinois I use university
rooms for talks. People outside my university can't (at least not as
easily).  The editor of the student paper here can decide what
articles go in the paper. Others can't.

What it doesn't allow is summary expulsion from forums for those who
qualify for access.

