For everyone who is worried that a minor nuisance has been hammered by an
out-of-control system, fear not. The McElwaine fandango has been going on
for years. His sysadmins were fed up with him long before this newsgroup
got created, and legal authorities were involved for a long time (as I
understood it, he got the courts involved in undoing a previous suspension
of posting privileges).

Don't worry that Bob wasn't warned that he was doing something wrong; he was,
repeatedly. He chose to ignore all warnings and subvert the system that UWEC
had in place (by involving external authorities). His behaviour over the years
did not improve, it worsened. If you want to look for a case of an unfeeling,
itching-for-a-fight system hammering an innocent victim, look elsewhere. This
was a case of a university going to extraordinary lengths to do everything by
the numbers before removing access from an individual who was abusing his
network access privileges.
